      "html": "<p>This species prefers to swim in schools more than other Pyrrhulinas, so it is an ideal community fish for the upper water column.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/pyrrhulina_lugubris_en/",
      "html": "<p>Regarding the coloration this Pyrrhulina may look a bit inconspicuous at first glimpse, but if the fish is given a chance to settle down it develops a bright, beautiful pastel coloration. In any other respect this fish is a true Pyrrhulina and enables many interesting observations in the aquarium.</p><p>Suggested common name: Pastel-Pyrrhulina.</p>"
